#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:120
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-access-tokens\">[`access-tokens`](#conf-access-tokens)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:122
msgid ""
"Access tokens used to access protected GitHub, GitLab, or other locations "
"requiring token-based authentication."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:125
msgid ""
"Access tokens are specified as a string made up of space-separated "
"`host=token` values.  The specific token used is selected by matching the "
"`host` portion against the \"host\" specification of the input. The `host` "
"portion may contain a path element which matches against the prefix URL for "
"the input. (eg: `github.com/org=token`). The actual use of the `token` value "
"is determined by the type of resource being accessed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:134
msgid ""
"Github: the token value is the OAUTH-TOKEN string obtained as the Personal "
"Access Token from the Github server (see https://docs.github.com/en/"
"developers/apps/building-oauth-apps/authorizing-oauth-apps)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:138
msgid ""
"Gitlab: the token value is either the OAuth2 token or the Personal Access "
"Token (these are different types tokens for gitlab, see https://docs.gitlab."
"com/12.10/ee/api/README.html#authentication). The `token` value should be "
"`type:tokenstring` where `type` is either `OAuth2` or `PAT` to indicate "
"which type of token is being specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:146
msgid "Example `~/.config/nix/nix.conf`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:152
msgid "Example `~/code/flake.nix`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:154
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"input.foo = {\n"
"  type = \"gitlab\";\n"
"  host = \"gitlab.mycompany.com\";\n"
"  owner = \"mycompany\";\n"
"  repo = \"pro\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:163
msgid ""
"This example specifies three tokens, one each for accessing github.com, "
"gitlab.mycompany.com, and gitlab.com."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:166
msgid ""
"The `input.foo` uses the \"gitlab\" fetcher, which might requires specifying "
"the token type along with the token value."
msgstr ""

