#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:178
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allow-dirty-locks\">[`allow-dirty-locks`](#conf-allow-dirty-"
"locks)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:195
msgid ""
"Whether to allow dirty inputs (such as dirty Git workdirs) to be locked via "
"their NAR hash. This is generally bad practice since Nix has no way to "
"obtain such inputs if they are subsequently modified. Therefore lock files "
"with dirty locks should generally only be used for local testing, and should "
"not be pushed to other users."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:204
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allow-import-from-derivation\">[`allow-import-from-"
"derivation`](#conf-allow-import-from-derivation)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:206 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1928
msgid ""
"By default, Nix allows [Import from Derivation](../language/import-from-"
"derivation.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:208
msgid ""
"With this option set to `false`, Nix throws an error when evaluating an "
"expression that uses this feature, even when the required store object is "
"readily available. This ensures that evaluation doesn't require any builds "
"to take place, regardless of the state of the store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:215
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allow-new-privileges\">[`allow-new-privileges`](#conf-allow-"
"new-privileges)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:217
msgid ""
"(Linux-specific.) By default, builders on Linux cannot acquire new "
"privileges by calling setuid/setgid programs or programs that have file "
"capabilities. For example, programs such as `sudo` or `ping` should fail. "
"(Note that in sandbox builds, no such programs are available unless you bind-"
"mount them into the sandbox via the `sandbox-paths` option.) You can allow "
"the use of such programs by enabling this option. This is impure and usually "
"undesirable, but may be useful in certain scenarios (e.g. to spin up "
"containers or set up userspace network interfaces in tests)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:229
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allow-symlinked-store\">[`allow-symlinked-store`](#conf-"
"allow-symlinked-store)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:231
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, Nix stops complaining if the store directory (typically `/"
"nix/store`) contains symlink components."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:234
msgid ""
"This risks making some builds \"impure\" because builders sometimes "
"\"canonicalise\" paths by resolving all symlink components. Problems occur "
"if those builds are then deployed to machines where /nix/store resolves to a "
"different location from that of the build machine. You can enable this "
"setting if you are sure you're not going to do that."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:242
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allow-unsafe-native-code-during-evaluation\">[`allow-unsafe-"
"native-code-during-evaluation`](#conf-allow-unsafe-native-code-during-"
"evaluation)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:244
msgid "Enable built-in functions that allow executing native code."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:246
msgid "In particular, this adds:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:247
msgid "`builtins.importNative` _path_ _symbol_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:249
msgid ""
"Opens dynamic shared object (DSO) at _path_, loads the function with the "
"symbol name _symbol_ from it and runs it. The loaded function must have the "
"following signature:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:252
msgid "\"C\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:255
msgid ""
"The [Nix C++ API documentation](../development/documentation.md#api-"
"documentation) has more details on evaluator internals."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:257
msgid "`builtins.exec` _arguments_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:259
msgid ""
"Execute a program, where _arguments_ are specified as a list of strings, and "
"parse its output as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:263
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allowed-impure-host-deps\">[`allowed-impure-host-deps`]"
"(#conf-allowed-impure-host-deps)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:265
msgid ""
"Which prefixes to allow derivations to ask for access to (primarily for "
"Darwin)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:269
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allowed-uris\">[`allowed-uris`](#conf-allowed-uris)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:271
msgid ""
"A list of URI prefixes to which access is allowed in restricted evaluation "
"mode. For example, when set to `https://github.com/NixOS`, builtin functions "
"such as `fetchGit` are allowed to access `https://github.com/NixOS/patchelf."
"git`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:276
msgid "Access is granted when"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:277
msgid "the URI is equal to the prefix,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:278
msgid "or the URI is a subpath of the prefix,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:279
msgid ""
"or the prefix is a URI scheme ended by a colon `:` and the URI has the same "
"scheme."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:283
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-allowed-users\">[`allowed-users`](#conf-allowed-users)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:285
msgid ""
"A list of user names, separated by whitespace. These users are allowed to "
"connect to the Nix daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:288
msgid ""
"You can specify groups by prefixing names with `@`. For instance, `@wheel` "
"means all users in the `wheel` group. Also, you can allow all users by "
"specifying `*`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:292 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:520
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:602 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1275
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1388 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1424
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:294
msgid ""
"Trusted users (set in [`trusted-users`](#conf-trusted-users)) can always "
"connect to the Nix daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:296
msgid "**Default:** `*`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:298
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-always-allow-substitutes\">[`always-allow-substitutes`]"
"(#conf-always-allow-substitutes)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:300
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, Nix ignores the [`allowSubstitutes`](../language/advanced-"
"attributes.md) attribute in derivations and always attempt to use [available "
"substituters](#conf-substituters)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:304
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-auto-allocate-uids\">[`auto-allocate-uids`](#conf-auto-"
"allocate-uids)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:311
msgid ""
"To change this setting, make sure the [`auto-allocate-uids` experimental "
"feature](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-auto-allocate-"
"uids) is enabled. For example, include the following in [`nix.conf`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:321
msgid ""
"Whether to select UIDs for builds automatically, instead of using the users "
"in `build-users-group`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:324
msgid ""
"UIDs are allocated starting at 872415232 (0x34000000) on Linux and 56930 on "
"macOS."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:328
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-auto-optimise-store\">[`auto-optimise-store`](#conf-auto-"
"optimise-store)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:330
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, Nix automatically detects files in the store that have "
"identical contents, and replaces them with hard links to a single copy. This "
"saves disk space. If set to `false` (the default), you can still run `nix-"
"store --optimise` to get rid of duplicate files."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:338
msgid "<span id=\"conf-bash-prompt\">[`bash-prompt`](#conf-bash-prompt)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:340
msgid "The bash prompt (`PS1`) in `nix develop` shells."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:344
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-bash-prompt-prefix\">[`bash-prompt-prefix`](#conf-bash-"
"prompt-prefix)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:346
msgid ""
"Prefix prepended to the `PS1` environment variable in `nix develop` shells."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:350
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-bash-prompt-suffix\">[`bash-prompt-suffix`](#conf-bash-"
"prompt-suffix)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:352
msgid ""
"Suffix appended to the `PS1` environment variable in `nix develop` shells."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:356
msgid "<span id=\"conf-build-dir\">[`build-dir`](#conf-build-dir)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:358
msgid ""
"Override the `build-dir` store setting for all stores that have this setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:360
msgid ""
"See also the per-store [`build-dir`](../store/types/local-store.md#store-"
"local-store-build-dir) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:362 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:663
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1080
msgid "**Default:** \\``"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:364
msgid "<span id=\"conf-build-hook\">[`build-hook`](#conf-build-hook)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:366
