msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:419
msgid "<span id=\"conf-builders\">[`builders`](#conf-builders)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:421
msgid "A semicolon- or newline-separated list of build machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:423
msgid ""
"In addition to the [usual ways of setting configuration options](../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md), the value can be read from a file by prefixing its "
"absolute path with `@`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:425 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:439
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:449 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:455
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:462 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:485
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:493
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:427
msgid "This is the default setting:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:433
msgid ""
"Each machine specification consists of the following elements, separated by "
"spaces. Only the first element is required. To leave a field at its default, "
"set it to `-`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:437
msgid ""
"The URI of the remote store in the format `ssh://[username@]hostname[:port]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:441
msgid "`ssh://nix@mac`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:443
msgid ""
"For backward compatibility, `ssh://` may be omitted. The hostname may be an "
"alias defined in `~/.ssh/config`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:446
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of [Nix system types](../development/building."
"md#system-type). If omitted, this defaults to the local platform type."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:451 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1817
msgid "`aarch64-darwin`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:453
msgid "It is possible for a machine to support multiple platform types."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:457
msgid "`i686-linux,x86_64-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:459
msgid ""
"The SSH identity file to be used to log in to the remote machine. If "
"omitted, SSH uses its regular identities."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:464
msgid "`/home/user/.ssh/id_mac`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:466
msgid ""
"The maximum number of builds that Nix executes in parallel on the machine. "
"Typically this should be equal to the number of CPU cores."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:469
msgid ""
"The “speed factor”, indicating the relative speed of the machine as a "
"positive integer or decimal number. If there are multiple machines of the "
"right type, Nix prefers the fastest, taking load into account."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:472
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of supported [system features](#conf-system-features)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:474
msgid ""
"A machine is only used to build a derivation if all the features in the "
"derivation's [`requiredSystemFeatures`](../language/advanced-attributes."
"html#adv-attr-requiredSystemFeatures) attribute are supported by that "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:476
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of required [system features](#conf-system-features)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:478
msgid ""
"A machine is only used to build a derivation if all of the machine’s "
"required features appear in the derivation’s [`requiredSystemFeatures`](../"
"language/advanced-attributes.html#adv-attr-requiredSystemFeatures) attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:480
msgid ""
"The (base64-encoded) public host key of the remote machine. If omitted, SSH "
"uses its regular `known_hosts` file."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:483
msgid "The value for this field can be obtained via `base64 -w0`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:487
msgid "Multiple builders specified on the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:489
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"--builders 'ssh://mac x86_64-darwin ; ssh://beastie x86_64-freebsd'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:495
msgid "This specifies several machines that can perform `i686-linux` builds:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:503
msgid "However, `poochie` only builds derivations that have the attribute"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:505
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"requiredSystemFeatures = [ \"benchmark\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:509
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:511
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"requiredSystemFeatures = [ \"benchmark\" \"kvm\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:515
msgid ""
"`itchy` cannot do builds that require `kvm`, but `scratchy` does support "
"such builds. For regular builds, `itchy` is preferred over `scratchy` "
"because it has a higher speed factor."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:518
msgid ""
"For Nix to use substituters, the calling user must be in the [`trusted-"
"users`](#conf-trusted-users) list."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:522
msgid ""
"A build machine must be accessible via SSH and have Nix installed. `nix` "
"must be available in `$PATH` for the user connecting over SSH."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:527
msgid ""
"If you are building via the Nix daemon (default), the Nix daemon user "
"account on the local machine (that is, `root`) requires access to a user "
"account on the remote machine (not necessarily `root`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:529
msgid ""
"If you can’t or don’t want to configure `root` to be able to access the "
"remote machine, set [`store`](#conf-store) to any [local store](../store/"
"types/local-store.html), e.g. by passing `--store /tmp` to the command on "
"the local machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:531
msgid ""
"To build only on remote machines and disable local builds, set [`max-jobs`]"
"(#conf-max-jobs) to 0."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:533
msgid ""
"If you want the remote machines to use substituters, set [`builders-use-"
"substitutes`](#conf-builders-use-substitutes) to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:537
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-builders-use-substitutes\">[`builders-use-substitutes`]"
"(#conf-builders-use-substitutes)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:539
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, Nix instructs [remote build machines](#conf-builders) to "
"use their own [`substituters`](#conf-substituters) if available."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:541
msgid ""
"It means that remote build hosts fetch as many dependencies as possible from "
"their own substituters (e.g, from `cache.nixos.org`) instead of waiting for "
"the local machine to upload them all. This can drastically reduce build "
"times if the network connection between the local machine and the remote "
"build host is slow."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:546
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-commit-lock-file-summary\">[`commit-lock-file-summary`]"
"(#conf-commit-lock-file-summary)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:563
msgid ""
"The commit summary to use when committing changed flake lock files. If "
"empty, the summary is generated based on the action performed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:568
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `commit-lockfile-summary`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:570
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-compress-build-log\">[`compress-build-log`](#conf-compress-"
"build-log)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:572
msgid ""
"If set to `true` (the default), build logs written to `/nix/var/log/nix/"
"drvs` are compressed on the fly using bzip2. Otherwise, they are not "
"compressed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:578
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-compress-log`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:580
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-connect-timeout\">[`connect-timeout`](#conf-connect-"
"timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:582
msgid ""
"The timeout (in seconds) for establishing connections in the binary cache "
"substituter. It corresponds to `curl`’s `--connect-timeout` option. A value "
"of 0 means no limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:586
msgid "**Default:** `15`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:588
msgid "<span id=\"conf-cores\">[`cores`](#conf-cores)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:590
msgid ""
"Sets the value of the `NIX_BUILD_CORES` environment variable in the "
"[invocation of the `builder` executable](../store/building.md#env-vars) of a "
"derivation. The `builder` executable can use this variable to control its "
"own maximum amount of parallelism."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:598
msgid ""
"For instance, in Nixpkgs, if the attribute `enableParallelBuilding` for the "
"`mkDerivation` build helper is set to `true`, it passes the `-"
"j${NIX_BUILD_CORES}` flag to GNU Make."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:600
msgid ""
"If set to `0`, nix will detect the number of CPU cores and pass this number "
"via `NIX_BUILD_CORES`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:604
msgid ""
"The number of parallel local Nix build jobs is independently controlled with "
"the [`max-jobs`](#conf-max-jobs) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:606 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:678
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1249 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1298
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1319 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1903
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2100
msgid "**Default:** `0`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:608
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-cores`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:610
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-debugger-on-trace\">[`debugger-on-trace`](#conf-debugger-on-"
"trace)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:612
msgid ""
"If set to true and the `--debugger` flag is given, the following functions "
"enter the debugger like [`builtins.break`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-"
"break):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:615
msgid "[`builtins.trace`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-trace)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:616
msgid ""
"[`builtins.traceVerbose`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-traceVerbose) if "
"[`trace-verbose`](#conf-trace-verbose) is set to true."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:618
msgid "[`builtins.warn`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-warn)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:620 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:629
msgid "This is useful for debugging warnings in third-party Nix code."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:624
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-debugger-on-warn\">[`debugger-on-warn`](#conf-debugger-on-"
"warn)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:626
msgid ""
"If set to true and the `--debugger` flag is given, [`builtins.warn`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-warn) will enter the debugger like [`builtins."
"break`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-break)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:631
msgid ""
"Use [`debugger-on-trace`](#conf-debugger-on-trace) to also enter the "
"debugger on legacy warnings that are logged with [`builtins.trace`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-trace)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:635
msgid "<span id=\"conf-diff-hook\">[`diff-hook`](#conf-diff-hook)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:637
msgid ""
"Absolute path to an executable capable of diffing build results. The hook is "
"executed if `run-diff-hook` is true, and the output of a build is known to "
"not be the same. This program is not executed to determine if two results "
"are the same."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:642
msgid ""
"The diff hook is executed by the same user and group who ran the build. "
"However, the diff hook does not have write access to the store path just "
"built."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:646
msgid "The diff hook program receives three parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:648
msgid "A path to the previous build's results"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:650
msgid "A path to the current build's results"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:652
msgid "The path to the build's derivation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:654
msgid ""
"The path to the build's scratch directory. This directory exists only if the "
"build was run with `--keep-failed`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:657
msgid ""
"The stderr and stdout output from the diff hook isn't displayed to the user. "
"Instead, it prints to the nix-daemon's log."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:660
msgid ""
"When using the Nix daemon, `diff-hook` must be set in the `nix.conf` "
"configuration file, and cannot be passed at the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:665
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-download-buffer-size\">[`download-buffer-size`](#conf-"
"download-buffer-size)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:667
msgid ""
"The size of Nix's internal download buffer in bytes during `curl` transfers. "
"If data is not processed quickly enough to exceed the size of this buffer, "
"downloads may stall. The default is 1048576 (1 MiB)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:671
msgid "**Default:** `1048576`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:673
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-download-speed\">[`download-speed`](#conf-download-speed)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:675
msgid ""
"Specify the maximum transfer rate in kilobytes per second you want Nix to "
"use for downloads."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:680
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-eval-attrset-update-layer-rhs-threshold\">[`eval-attrset-"
"update-layer-rhs-threshold`](#conf-eval-attrset-update-layer-rhs-threshold)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:682
msgid ""
"Tunes the maximum size of an attribute set that, when used as a right "
"operand in an [attribute set update expression](../language/operators."
"md#update), uses a more space-efficient linked-list representation of "
"attribute sets."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:686
msgid ""
"Setting this to larger values generally leads to less memory allocations, "
"but may lead to worse evaluation performance."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:689
msgid "A value of `0` disables this optimization completely."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:691
msgid ""
"This is an advanced performance tuning option and typically should not be "
"changed. The default value is chosen to balance performance and memory "
"usage. On 32 bit systems where memory is scarce, the default is a large "
"value to reduce the amount of allocations."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:695 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1308
msgid "**Default:** `16`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:697
msgid "<span id=\"conf-eval-cache\">[`eval-cache`](#conf-eval-cache)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:699
msgid ""
"Whether to use the flake evaluation cache. Certain commands won't have to "
"evaluate when invoked for the second time with a particular version of a "
"flake. Intermediate results are not cached."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:705
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-eval-profile-file\">[`eval-profile-file`](#conf-eval-profile-"
"file)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:707
msgid ""
"Specifies the file where [evaluation profile](#conf-eval-profiler) is saved."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:709
msgid "**Default:** `nix.profile`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:711
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-eval-profiler\">[`eval-profiler`](#conf-eval-profiler)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:713
msgid "Enables evaluation profiling. The following modes are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:715
msgid ""
"`flamegraph` stack sampling profiler. Outputs folded format, one line per "
"stack (suitable for `flamegraph.pl` and compatible tools)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:717
msgid ""
"Use [`eval-profile-file`](#conf-eval-profile-file) to specify where the "
"profile is saved."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:719
msgid "See [Using the `eval-profiler`](../advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:721
msgid "**Default:** `disabled`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:723
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-eval-profiler-frequency\">[`eval-profiler-frequency`](#conf-"
"eval-profiler-frequency)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:725
msgid ""
"Specifies the sampling rate in hertz for sampling evaluation profilers. Use "
"`0` to sample the stack after each function call. See [`eval-profiler`]"
"(#conf-eval-profiler)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:729
msgid "**Default:** `99`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:731
msgid "<span id=\"conf-eval-system\">[`eval-system`](#conf-eval-system)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:733
msgid ""
"This option defines [`builtins.currentSystem`](../language/builtins."
"md#builtins-currentSystem) in the Nix language if it is set as a non-empty "
"string. Otherwise, if it is defined as the empty string (the default), the "
"value of the [`system` ](#conf-system) configuration setting is used instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:740
msgid ""
"Unlike `system`, this setting does not change what kind of derivations can "
"be built locally. This is useful for evaluating Nix code on one system to "
"produce derivations to be built on another type of system."
msgstr ""

