"<span id=\"conf-extra-platforms\">[`extra-platforms`](#conf-extra-"
"platforms)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:832
msgid "System types of executables that can be run on this machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:834
msgid ""
"Nix only builds a given [store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation) locally when its `system` attribute equals any of the values "
"specified here or in the [`system` option](#conf-system)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:836
msgid ""
"Setting this can be useful to build derivations locally on compatible "
"machines:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:837
msgid ""
"`i686-linux` executables can be run on `x86_64-linux` machines (set by "
"default)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:838
msgid ""
"`x86_64-darwin` executables can be run on macOS `aarch64-darwin` with "
"Rosetta 2 (set by default where applicable)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:839
msgid "`armv6` and `armv5tel` executables can be run on `armv7`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:840
msgid "some `aarch64` machines can also natively run 32-bit ARM code"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:841
msgid ""
"`qemu-user` may be used to support non-native platforms (though this may be "
"slow and buggy)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:844
msgid ""
"Build systems usually detect the target platform to be the current physical "
"system and therefore produce machine code incompatible with what may be "
"intended in the derivation. You should design your derivation's `builder` "
"accordingly and cross-check the results when using this option against "
"natively-built versions of your derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:849
msgid "<span id=\"conf-fallback\">[`fallback`](#conf-fallback)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:851
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, Nix falls back to building from source if a binary "
"substitute fails. This is equivalent to the `--fallback` flag. The default "
"is `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:857
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-fallback`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:859
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-filetransfer-retry-attempts\">[`filetransfer-retry-attempts`]"
"(#conf-filetransfer-retry-attempts)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:861
msgid ""
"The number of times Nix attempts a file transfer (download or upload) before "
"giving up. Retries apply to transient failures: connection-level errors, "
"HTTP 408, 429, and most 5xx responses. Authentication failures "
"(401/403/407), 404/410, and other 4xx responses are not retried."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:869
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `download-attempts`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:871
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-filetransfer-retry-delay\">[`filetransfer-retry-delay`]"
"(#conf-filetransfer-retry-delay)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:873
msgid ""
"Initial delay in milliseconds before retrying a failed file transfer "
"(download or upload). The delay doubles with each subsequent attempt "
"(exponential backoff) and is subject to random jitter (see `filetransfer-"
"retry-jitter`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:878
msgid "**Default:** `100`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:880
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-filetransfer-retry-delay-rate-limited\">[`filetransfer-retry-"
"delay-rate-limited`](#conf-filetransfer-retry-delay-rate-limited)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:882
msgid ""
"Initial delay in milliseconds before retrying a file transfer that failed "
"with a rate-limit response (HTTP 429 or 503). The delay doubles with each "
"subsequent attempt."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:886
msgid ""
"Servers may send a `Retry-After` header specifying a longer delay; when "
"present, Nix respects the larger of the two values."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:889
msgid "**Default:** `5000`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:891
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-filetransfer-retry-jitter\">[`filetransfer-retry-jitter`]"
"(#conf-filetransfer-retry-jitter)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:893
msgid ""
"Whether to apply random jitter to retry delays. When enabled, each retry "
"waits for a random duration between 0 and the computed delay (\"full "
"jitter\"), which spreads out retry storms from many clients."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:897
msgid "Disable for deterministic retry timing (primarily useful for tests)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:901
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-filetransfer-retry-max-delay\">[`filetransfer-retry-max-"
"delay`](#conf-filetransfer-retry-max-delay)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:903
msgid ""
"Ceiling on the exponential backoff delay in milliseconds. This does not cap "
"server-provided `Retry-After` values, which are honored as-is."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:906
msgid "**Default:** `60000`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:908
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-filter-syscalls\">[`filter-syscalls`](#conf-filter-"
"syscalls)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:910
msgid ""
"Whether to prevent certain dangerous system calls, such as creation of "
"setuid/setgid files or adding ACLs or extended attributes. Only disable this "
"if you're aware of the security implications."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:917
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-flake-registry\">[`flake-registry`](#conf-flake-registry)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:934
msgid "Path or URI of the global flake registry."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:936
msgid "When empty, disables the global flake registry."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:938
msgid "**Default:** `https://channels.nixos.org/flake-registry.json`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:940
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-fsync-metadata\">[`fsync-metadata`](#conf-fsync-metadata)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:942
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, changes to the Nix store metadata (in `/nix/var/nix/db`) "
"are synchronously flushed to disk. This improves robustness in case of "
"system crashes, but reduces performance. The default is `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:949
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-fsync-store-paths\">[`fsync-store-paths`](#conf-fsync-store-"
"paths)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:951
msgid ""
"Whether to call `fsync()` on store paths before registering them, to flush "
"them to disk. This improves robustness in case of system crashes, but "
"reduces performance. The default is `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:957
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-gc-reserved-space\">[`gc-reserved-space`](#conf-gc-reserved-"
"space)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:959
msgid "Amount of reserved disk space for the garbage collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:961 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1015
msgid "**Default:** `8388608`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:963
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-hashed-mirrors\">[`hashed-mirrors`](#conf-hashed-mirrors)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:965
msgid ""
"A list of web servers used by `builtins.fetchurl` to obtain files by hash. "
"Given a hash algorithm _ha_ and a base-16 hash _h_, Nix tries to download "
"the file from _hashed-mirror_/_ha_/_h_. This allows files to be downloaded "
"even if they have disappeared from their original URI. For example, given an "
"example mirror `http://tarballs.nixos.org/`, when building the derivation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:972
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchurl {\n"
"  url = \"https://example.org/foo-1.2.3.tar.xz\";\n"
"  sha256 = "
"\"2c26b46b68ffc68ff99b453c1d30413413422d706483bfa0f98a5e886266e7ae\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:979
msgid ""
"Nix will attempt to download this file from `http://tarballs.nixos.org/"
"sha256/2c26b46b68ffc68ff99b453c1d30413413422d706483bfa0f98a5e886266e7ae` "
"first. If it is not available there, it tries the original URI."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:985
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-http-connections\">[`http-connections`](#conf-http-"
"connections)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:987
msgid ""
"The maximum number of parallel TCP connections used to fetch files from "
"binary caches and by other downloads. It defaults to 25. 0 means no limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:991 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1241
msgid "**Default:** `25`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:993
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `binary-caches-parallel-connections`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:995
msgid "<span id=\"conf-http2\">[`http2`](#conf-http2)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:997
msgid "Whether to enable HTTP/2 support."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1001
msgid "<span id=\"conf-http3\">[`http3`](#conf-http3)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1003
msgid ""
"Whether to try enabling HTTP/3 (QUIC). When enabled, Nix requests HTTP/3 and "
"transparently falls back to HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1 for servers that do not "
"support it. This option has no effect unless the `nix` binary is linked "
"against a libcurl built with HTTP/3 (QUIC) support."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1011
msgid "<span id=\"conf-id-count\">[`id-count`](#conf-id-count)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1013
msgid "The number of UIDs/GIDs to use for dynamic ID allocation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1017
msgid "<span id=\"conf-ignore-try\">[`ignore-try`](#conf-ignore-try)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1019
msgid ""
"If set to true, ignore exceptions inside 'tryEval' calls when evaluating Nix "
"expressions in debug mode (using the --debugger flag). By default the "
"debugger pauses on all exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1024
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-ignored-acls\">[`ignored-acls`](#conf-ignored-acls)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1026
msgid ""
"A list of ACLs that should be ignored, normally Nix attempts to remove all "
"ACLs from files and directories in the Nix store, but some ACLs like "
"`security.selinux` or `system.nfs4_acl` can't be removed even by root. "
"Therefore it's best to just ignore them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1031
msgid "**Default:** `security.csm security.selinux system.nfs4_acl`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1033
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-impersonate-linux-26\">[`impersonate-linux-26`](#conf-"
"impersonate-linux-26)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1035
msgid "Whether to impersonate a Linux 2.6 machine on newer kernels."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1039
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-impersonate-linux-26`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1041
msgid "<span id=\"conf-impure-env\">[`impure-env`](#conf-impure-env)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1048
msgid ""
"To change this setting, make sure the [`configurable-impure-env` "
"experimental feature](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-"
"configurable-impure-env) is enabled. For example, include the following in "
"[`nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1058
msgid "A list of items, each in the format of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1060
msgid "`name=value`: Set environment variable `name` to `value`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1062
msgid ""
"If the user is trusted (see `trusted-users` option), when building a fixed-"
"output derivation, environment variables set in this option is passed to the "
"builder if they are listed in [`impureEnvVars`](../language/advanced-"
"attributes.md#adv-attr-impureEnvVars)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1066
msgid ""
"This option is useful for, e.g., setting `https_proxy` for fixed-output "
"derivations and in a multi-user Nix installation, or setting private access "
"tokens when fetching a private repository."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1072
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-json-log-path\">[`json-log-path`](#conf-json-log-path)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1074
msgid ""
"A file or unix socket to which JSON records of Nix's log output are written, "
"in the same format as `--log-format internal-json` (without the `@nix ` "
"prefixes on each line). Concurrent writes to the same file by multiple Nix "
"processes are not supported and may result in interleaved or corrupted log "
"records."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1082
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-keep-build-log\">[`keep-build-log`](#conf-keep-build-log)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1084
msgid ""
"If set to `true` (the default), Nix writes the build log of a derivation (i."
"e. the standard output and error of its builder) to the directory `/nix/var/"
"log/nix/drvs`. The build log can be retrieved using the command `nix-store -"
"l path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1091
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-keep-log`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1093
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-keep-derivations\">[`keep-derivations`](#conf-keep-"
"derivations)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1095
msgid ""
"If `true` (default), the garbage collector keeps the derivations from which "
"non-garbage store paths were built. If `false`, they are deleted unless "
"explicitly registered as a root (or reachable from other roots)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1100
msgid ""
"Keeping derivation around is useful for querying and traceability (e.g., it "
"allows you to ask with what dependencies or options a store path was built), "
"so by default this option is on. Turn it off to save a bit of disk space (or "
"a lot if `keep-outputs` is also turned on)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1106 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1160
msgid ""
"This option only applies to garbage collection of the whole store and does "
"not affect deleting explicit paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1111
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `gc-keep-derivations`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1113
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-keep-env-derivations\">[`keep-env-derivations`](#conf-keep-"
"env-derivations)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1115
msgid ""
"If `false` (default), derivations are not stored in Nix user environments. "
"That is, the derivations of any build-time-only dependencies may be garbage-"
"collected."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1119
msgid ""
"If `true`, when you add a Nix derivation to a user environment, the path of "
"the derivation is stored in the user environment. Thus, the derivation isn't "
"garbage-collected until the user environment generation is deleted (`nix-env "
"--delete-generations`). To prevent build-time-only dependencies from being "
"collected, you should also turn on `keep-outputs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1126
msgid ""
"The difference between this option and `keep-derivations` is that this one "
"is \"sticky\": it applies to any user environment created while this option "
"was enabled, while `keep-derivations` only applies at the moment the garbage "
"collector is run."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1133
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `env-keep-derivations`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1135
msgid "<span id=\"conf-keep-failed\">[`keep-failed`](#conf-keep-failed)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1137
msgid "Whether to keep temporary directories of failed builds."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1141
msgid "<span id=\"conf-keep-going\">[`keep-going`](#conf-keep-going)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1143
msgid "Whether to keep building derivations when another build fails."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1147
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-keep-outputs\">[`keep-outputs`](#conf-keep-outputs)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1149
msgid ""
"If `true`, the garbage collector keeps the outputs of non-garbage "
"derivations. If `false` (default), outputs are deleted unless they are GC "
"roots themselves (or reachable from other roots)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1154
msgid ""
"In general, outputs must be registered as roots separately. However, even if "
"the output of a derivation is registered as a root, the collector still "
"deletes store paths that are used only at build time (e.g., the C compiler, "
"or source tarballs downloaded from the network). To prevent it from doing "
"so, set this option to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1165
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `gc-keep-outputs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1167
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-lint-absolute-path-literals\">[`lint-absolute-path-literals`]"
"(#conf-lint-absolute-path-literals)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1169
msgid ""
"Controls handling of absolute path literals (paths starting with `/`) and "
"home path literals (paths starting with `~/`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1171 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1192
msgid "`ignore`: Ignore without warning (default)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1172
msgid "`warn`: Emit a warning about non-portability"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1173 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1194
msgid "`fatal`: Treat as a parse error"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1175
msgid ""
"It is true that some files are more difficult to reference with relative "
"paths, because they would require lots of `../../..` upward traversing to "
"reach them. But firstly, it is probably not a good idea to reference these "
"files --- such paths often make Nix expressions less portable and "
"reproducible, as they depend on the file system layout of the machine "
"evaluating the expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1181
msgid ""
"Secondly, with [pure evaluation mode](#conf-pure-eval), most such files are "
"prohibited to access anyway, whether by absolute or relative paths. In that "
"case, enabling this lint in fatal mode is less disruptive, because the paths "
"pure eval allows are usually not the ones that would be ergonomically "
"expressed with absolute paths anyway."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1186 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1202
#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1235
msgid "**Default:** `ignore`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1188
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-lint-short-path-literals\">[`lint-short-path-literals`]"
"(#conf-lint-short-path-literals)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1190
msgid ""
"Controls handling of relative path literals that don't start with `./` or "
"`../`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1193
msgid "`warn`: Emit a warning suggesting to use `./` prefix"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1196
msgid ""
"For example, with this setting set to `warn` or `fatal`, `foo/bar` would "
"suggest using `./foo/bar` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1199
msgid ""
"This is useful for improving code readability and making path literals more "
"explicit."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1204
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-lint-url-literals\">[`lint-url-literals`](#conf-lint-url-"
"literals)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1206
msgid ""
"Controls handling of unquoted URLs as part of the Nix language syntax. The "
"Nix language allows for URL literals, like so:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1209
msgid ""
"```\n"
"$ nix repl\n"
"nix-repl> http://foo\n"
"\"http://foo\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1215
msgid ""
"Setting this to `warn` or `fatal` will cause the Nix parser to warn or throw "
"an error when encountering a URL literal:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1218
msgid ""
"```\n"
"$ nix repl --lint-url-literals fatal\n"
"nix-repl> http://foo\n"
"error: URL literal 'http://foo' is deprecated\n"
"       at «string»:1:1:\n"
"\n"
"            1| http://foo\n"
"             | ^\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1228
msgid "Unquoted URLs are being deprecated and their usage is discouraged."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1230
msgid ""
"The reason is that, as opposed to path literals, URLs have no special "
"properties that distinguish them from regular strings, URLs containing query "
"parameters have to be quoted anyway, and unquoted URLs may confuse external "
"tooling."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1237
msgid "<span id=\"conf-log-lines\">[`log-lines`](#conf-log-lines)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1239
msgid "The number of lines of the tail of the log to show if a build fails."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1243
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-max-build-log-size\">[`max-build-log-size`](#conf-max-build-"
"log-size)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1245
msgid ""
"This option defines the maximum number of bytes that a builder can write to "
"its stdout/stderr. If the builder exceeds this limit, it's killed. A value "
"of `0` (the default) means that there is no limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1251
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-max-log-size`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1253
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-max-call-depth\">[`max-call-depth`](#conf-max-call-depth)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1255
msgid "The maximum function call depth to allow before erroring."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1257
msgid "**Default:** `10000`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1259
msgid "<span id=\"conf-max-free\">[`max-free`](#conf-max-free)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1261
msgid ""
"When a garbage collection is triggered by the `min-free` option, it stops as "
"soon as `max-free` bytes are available. The default is infinity (i.e. delete "
"all garbage)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1265
msgid "**Default:** `9223372036854775807`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1267
msgid "<span id=\"conf-max-jobs\">[`max-jobs`](#conf-max-jobs)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1269
msgid "Maximum number of jobs that Nix tries to build locally in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1271
msgid ""
"The special value `auto` causes Nix to use the number of CPUs in your "
"system. Use `0` to disable local builds and directly use the remote machines "
"specified in [`builders`](#conf-builders). This doesn't affect derivations "
"that have [`preferLocalBuild = true`](../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-"
"attr-preferLocalBuild), which are always built locally."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1277
msgid ""
"The number of CPU cores to use for each build job is independently "
"determined by the [`cores`](#conf-cores) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1280
msgid ""
"The setting can be overridden using the `--max-jobs` (`-j`) command line "
"switch."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1282
msgid "**Default:** `1`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1284
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-max-jobs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1286
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-max-silent-time\">[`max-silent-time`](#conf-max-silent-"
"time)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1288
msgid ""
"This option defines the maximum number of seconds that a builder can go "
"without producing any data on standard output or standard error. This is "
"useful (for instance in an automated build system) to catch builds that are "
"stuck in an infinite loop, or to catch remote builds that are hanging due to "
"network problems. It can be overridden using the `--max-silent-time` command "
"line switch."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1295 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1900
msgid "The value `0` means that there is no timeout. This is also the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1300
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-max-silent-time`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1302
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-max-substitution-jobs\">[`max-substitution-jobs`](#conf-max-"
"substitution-jobs)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1304
msgid ""
"This option defines the maximum number of substitution jobs that Nix tries "
"to run in parallel. The default is `16`. The minimum value one can choose is "
"`1` and lower values are interpreted as `1`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1310
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `substitution-max-jobs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1312
msgid "<span id=\"conf-min-free\">[`min-free`](#conf-min-free)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1314
msgid ""
"When free disk space in `/nix/store` drops below `min-free` during a build, "
"Nix performs a garbage-collection until `max-free` bytes are available or "
"there is no more garbage. A value of `0` (the default) disables this feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1321
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-min-free-check-interval\">[`min-free-check-interval`](#conf-"
"min-free-check-interval)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1323
msgid "Number of seconds between checking free disk space."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1327
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-nar-buffer-size\">[`nar-buffer-size`](#conf-nar-buffer-"
"size)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1329
msgid "Maximum size of NARs before spilling them to disk."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1331
msgid "**Default:** `33554432`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1333
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-narinfo-cache-meta-ttl\">[`narinfo-cache-meta-ttl`](#conf-"
"narinfo-cache-meta-ttl)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1335
msgid ""
"The TTL in seconds for caching binary cache metadata (i.e. `/nix-cache-"
"info`). This determines how long information about a binary cache (such as "
"its store directory, priority, and whether it wants mass queries) is "
"considered valid before being refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1340
msgid "**Default:** `604800`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1342
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-narinfo-cache-negative-ttl\">[`narinfo-cache-negative-ttl`]"
"(#conf-narinfo-cache-negative-ttl)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1344
msgid ""
"The TTL in seconds for negative lookups. If a store path is queried from a "
"[substituter](#conf-substituters) but was not found, a negative lookup is "
"cached in the local disk cache database for the specified duration."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1347
msgid "Set to `0` to force updating the lookup cache."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1349
msgid "To wipe the lookup cache completely:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1356 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1890
msgid "**Default:** `3600`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1358
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-narinfo-cache-positive-ttl\">[`narinfo-cache-positive-ttl`]"
"(#conf-narinfo-cache-positive-ttl)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1360
msgid ""
"The TTL in seconds for positive lookups. If a store path is queried from a "
"substituter, the result of the query is cached in the local disk cache "
"database including some of the NAR metadata. The default TTL is a month, "
"setting a shorter TTL for positive lookups can be useful for binary caches "
"that have frequent garbage collection, in which case having a more frequent "
"cache invalidation would prevent trying to pull the path again and failing "
"with a hash mismatch if the build isn't reproducible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1369
msgid "**Default:** `2592000`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1371
msgid "<span id=\"conf-netrc-file\">[`netrc-file`](#conf-netrc-file)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1373
msgid ""
"If set to an absolute path to a `netrc` file, Nix uses the HTTP "
"authentication credentials in this file when trying to download from a "
"remote host through HTTP or HTTPS. Defaults to `$NIX_CONF_DIR/netrc`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1378
msgid ""
"The `netrc` file consists of a list of accounts in the following format:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1385
msgid ""
"For the exact syntax, see [the `curl` documentation](https://ec.haxx.se/"
"usingcurl-netrc.html)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1390
msgid ""
"This must be an absolute path, and `~` is not resolved. For example, `~/."
"netrc` won't resolve to your home directory's `.netrc`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1394
msgid "**Default:** `/dummy/netrc`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1396
msgid "<span id=\"conf-nix-path\">[`nix-path`](#conf-nix-path)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1398
msgid ""
"List of search paths to use for [lookup path](../language/constructs/lookup-"
"path.md) resolution. This setting determines the value of [`builtins."
"nixPath`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-nixPath) and can be used with "
"[`builtins.findFile`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-findFile)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1402
msgid ""
"The configuration setting is overridden by the [`NIX_PATH`](../command-ref/"
"env-common.md#env-NIX_PATH) environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1404
msgid ""
"`NIX_PATH` is overridden by [specifying the setting as the command line flag]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#command-line-flags) `--nix-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1405
msgid ""
"Any current value is extended by the [`-I` option](../command-ref/opt-common."
"md#opt-I) or `--extra-nix-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1407
msgid "If the respective paths are accessible, the default values are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1409
msgid "`$HOME/.nix-defexpr/channels`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1411
msgid ""
"The [user channel link](../command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md#user-"
"channel-link), pointing to the current state of [channels](../command-ref/"
"files/channels.md) for the current user."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1413
msgid "`nixpkgs=$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root/channels/nixpkgs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1415
msgid "The current state of the `nixpkgs` channel for the `root` user."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1417
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root/channels`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1419
msgid "The current state of all channels for the `root` user."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1421
msgid ""
"These files are set up by the [Nix installer](../installation/installing-"
"binary.md). See [`NIX_STATE_DIR`](../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_STATE_DIR) for details on the environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1426
msgid ""
"If [restricted evaluation](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-restrict-eval) "
"is enabled, the default value is empty."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1428
msgid ""
"If [pure evaluation](#conf-pure-eval) is enabled, `builtins.nixPath` "
"_always_ evaluates to the empty list `[ ]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1432
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-nix-shell-always-looks-for-shell-nix\">[`nix-shell-always-"
"looks-for-shell-nix`](#conf-nix-shell-always-looks-for-shell-nix)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1434
msgid ""
"Before Nix 2.24, [`nix-shell`](../command-ref/nix-shell.md) would only look "
"at `shell.nix` if it was in the working directory - when no file was "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1436
msgid ""
"Since Nix 2.24, `nix-shell` always looks for a `shell.nix`, whether that's "
"in the working directory, or in a directory that was passed as an argument."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1438 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1451
msgid ""
"You may set this to `false` to temporarily revert to the behavior of Nix "
"2.23 and older."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1440 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1453
msgid ""
"Using this setting is not recommended. It will be deprecated and removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1445
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-nix-shell-shebang-arguments-relative-to-script\">[`nix-shell-"
"shebang-arguments-relative-to-script`](#conf-nix-shell-shebang-arguments-"
"relative-to-script)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1447
msgid ""
"Before Nix 2.24, relative file path expressions in arguments in a `nix-"
"shell` shebang were resolved relative to the working directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1449
msgid ""
"Since Nix 2.24, `nix-shell` resolves these paths in a manner that is "
"relative to the [base directory](../glossary.md#gloss-base-directory), "
"defined as the script's directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1458
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-plugin-files\">[`plugin-files`](#conf-plugin-files)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1460
msgid ""
"A list of plugin files to be loaded by Nix. Each of these files is dlopened "
"by Nix. If they contain the symbol `nix_plugin_entry()`, this symbol is "
"called. Alternatively, they can affect execution through static "
"initialization. In particular, these plugins may construct static instances "
"of RegisterPrimOp to add new primops or constants to the expression "
"language, RegisterStoreImplementation to add new store implementations, "
"RegisterCommand to add new subcommands to the `nix` command, and "
"RegisterSetting to add new nix config settings. See the constructors for "
"those types for more details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1470
msgid ""
"Warning! These APIs are inherently unstable and may change from release to "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1473
msgid ""
"Since these files are loaded into the same address space as Nix itself, they "
"must be DSOs compatible with the instance of Nix running at the time (i.e. "
"compiled against the same headers, not linked to any incompatible "
"libraries). They should not be linked to any Nix libraries directly, as "
"those are already available at load time."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1480
msgid ""
"If an entry in the list is a directory, all files in the directory are "
"loaded as plugins (non-recursively)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1485
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-post-build-hook\">[`post-build-hook`](#conf-post-build-"
"hook)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1487
msgid "Optional. The path to a program to execute after each build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1489
msgid ""
"This option is only settable in the global `nix.conf`, or on the command "
"line by trusted users."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1492
msgid ""
"When using the nix-daemon, the daemon executes the hook as `root`. If the "
"nix-daemon is not involved, the hook runs as the user executing the nix-"
"build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1496
msgid "The hook executes after an evaluation-time build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1498
msgid "The hook does not execute on substituted paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1500
msgid "The hook's output always goes to the user's terminal."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1502
msgid "If the hook fails, the build succeeds but no further builds execute."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1505
msgid ""
"The hook executes synchronously, and blocks other builds from progressing "
"while it runs."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1508
msgid ""
"The program executes with no arguments. The program's environment contains "
"the following environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1511
msgid "`DRV_PATH` The derivation for the built paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1514
msgid "Example: `/nix/store/5nihn1a7pa8b25l9zafqaqibznlvvp3f-bash-4.4-p23.drv`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1517
msgid ""
"`OUT_PATHS` Output paths of the built derivation, separated by a space "
"character."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1521
msgid ""
"Example: `/nix/store/l88brggg9hpy96ijds34dlq4n8fan63g-bash-4.4-p23-dev /nix/"
"store/vch71bhyi5akr5zs40k8h2wqxx69j80l-bash-4.4-p23-doc /nix/store/"
"c5cxjywi66iwn9dcx5yvwjkvl559ay6p-bash-4.4-p23-info /nix/store/"
"scz72lskj03ihkcn42ias5mlp4i4gr1k-bash-4.4-p23-man /nix/store/"
"a724znygmd1cac856j3gfsyvih3lw07j-bash-4.4-p23`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1530
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-pre-build-hook\">[`pre-build-hook`](#conf-pre-build-hook)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1532
msgid ""
"If set, the path to a program that can set extra derivation-specific "
"settings for this system. This is used for settings that can't be captured "
"by the derivation model itself and are too variable between different "
"versions of the same system to be hard-coded into nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1537
msgid ""
"The hook is passed the derivation path and, if sandboxes are enabled, the "
"sandbox directory. It can then modify the sandbox and send a series of "
"commands to modify various settings to stdout. The currently recognized "
"commands are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1542
msgid ""
"`extra-sandbox-paths`  \n"
"Pass a list of files and directories to be included in the sandbox for this "
"build. One entry per line, terminated by an empty line. Entries have the "
"same format as `sandbox-paths`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1549
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-preallocate-contents\">[`preallocate-contents`](#conf-"
"preallocate-contents)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1551
msgid "Whether to preallocate files when writing objects with known size."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1555
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-print-missing\">[`print-missing`](#conf-print-missing)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1557
msgid "Whether to print what paths need to be built or downloaded."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1561
msgid "<span id=\"conf-pure-eval\">[`pure-eval`](#conf-pure-eval)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1563
msgid ""
"Pure evaluation mode ensures that the result of Nix expressions is fully "
"determined by explicitly declared inputs, and not influenced by external "
"state:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1565
msgid ""
"Restrict file system and network access to files specified by cryptographic "
"hash"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1566
msgid "Disable impure constants:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1567
msgid ""
"[`builtins.currentSystem`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-currentSystem)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1568
msgid "[`builtins.currentTime`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-currentTime)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1569
msgid "[`builtins.nixPath`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-nixPath)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1570
msgid "[`builtins.storePath`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-storePath)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1574
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-require-drop-supplementary-groups\">[`require-drop-"
"supplementary-groups`](#conf-require-drop-supplementary-groups)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1576
msgid ""
"Following the principle of least privilege, Nix attempts to drop "
"supplementary groups when building with sandboxing."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1579
msgid ""
"However this can fail under some circumstances. For example, if the user "
"lacks the `CAP_SETGID` capability. Search `setgroups(2)` for `EPERM` to find "
"more detailed information on this."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1583
msgid ""
"If you encounter such a failure, setting this option to `false` enables you "
"to ignore it and continue. But before doing so, you should consider the "
"security implications carefully. Not dropping supplementary groups means the "
"build sandbox is less restricted than intended."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1587
msgid ""
"This option defaults to `true` when the user is root (since `root` usually "
"has permissions to call setgroups) and `false` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1593
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-require-sigs\">[`require-sigs`](#conf-require-sigs)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1595
msgid ""
"If set to `true` (the default), any non-content-addressed path added or "
"copied to the Nix store (e.g. when substituting from a binary cache) must "
"have a signature by a trusted key. A trusted key is one listed in `trusted-"
"public-keys`, or a public key counterpart to a private key stored in a file "
"listed in `secret-key-files`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1601
msgid ""
"Set to `false` to disable signature checking and trust all non-content-"
"addressed paths unconditionally."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1604
msgid ""
"(Content-addressed paths are inherently trustworthy and thus unaffected by "
"this configuration option.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1609
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-restrict-eval\">[`restrict-eval`](#conf-restrict-eval)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1611
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the Nix evaluator doesn't allow access to any files "
"outside of [`builtins.nixPath`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-nixPath), "
"or to URIs outside of [`allowed-uris`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"allowed-uris)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1619
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-run-diff-hook\">[`run-diff-hook`](#conf-run-diff-hook)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1621
msgid "If true, enable the execution of the `diff-hook` program."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1623
msgid ""
"When using the Nix daemon, `run-diff-hook` must be set in the `nix.conf` "
"configuration file, and cannot be passed at the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1629
msgid "<span id=\"conf-sandbox\">[`sandbox`](#conf-sandbox)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1631
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, builds are performed in a _sandboxed environment_, i.e., "
"they're isolated from the normal file system hierarchy and only see their "
"dependencies in the Nix store, the temporary build directory, private "
"versions of `/proc`, `/dev`, `/dev/shm` and `/dev/pts` (on Linux), and the "
"paths configured with the `sandbox-paths` option. This is useful to prevent "
"undeclared dependencies on files in directories such as `/usr/bin`. In "
"addition, on Linux, builds run in private PID, mount, network, IPC and UTS "
"namespaces to isolate them from other processes in the system (except that "
"fixed-output derivations do not run in private network namespace to ensure "
"they can access the network)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1644
msgid ""
"Currently, sandboxing only work on Linux and macOS. The use of a sandbox "
"requires that Nix is run as root (so you should use the \"build users\" "
"feature to perform the actual builds under different users than root)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1649
msgid ""
"If this option is set to `relaxed`, then fixed-output derivations and "
"derivations that have the `__noChroot` attribute set to `true` do not run in "
"sandboxes."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1653
msgid "The default is `true` on Linux and `false` on all other platforms."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1657
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-use-chroot`, `build-use-sandbox`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1659
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-sandbox-build-dir\">[`sandbox-build-dir`](#conf-sandbox-"
"build-dir)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1661 source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1671
msgid "_Linux only_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1663
msgid "The build directory inside the sandbox."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1665
msgid "This directory is backed by [`build-dir`](#conf-build-dir) on the host."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1667
msgid "**Default:** `/build`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1669
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-sandbox-dev-shm-size\">[`sandbox-dev-shm-size`](#conf-"
"sandbox-dev-shm-size)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1673
msgid ""
"This option determines the maximum size of the `tmpfs` filesystem mounted on "
"`/dev/shm` in Linux sandboxes. For the format, see the description of the "
"`size` option of `tmpfs` in mount(8). The default is `50%`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1678
msgid "**Default:** `50%`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1680
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-sandbox-fallback\">[`sandbox-fallback`](#conf-sandbox-"
"fallback)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1682
msgid "Whether to disable sandboxing when the kernel doesn't allow it."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1686
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-sandbox-paths\">[`sandbox-paths`](#conf-sandbox-paths)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1688
msgid ""
"A list of paths bind-mounted into Nix sandbox environments. You can use the "
"syntax `target=source` to mount a path in a different location in the "
"sandbox; for instance, `/bin=/nix-bin` mounts the path `/nix-bin` as `/bin` "
"inside the sandbox. If _source_ is followed by `?`, then it is not an error "
"if _source_ does not exist; for example, `/dev/nvidiactl?` specifies that `/"
"dev/nvidiactl` only be mounted in the sandbox if it exists in the host "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1696
msgid ""
"If the source is in the Nix store, then its closure is added to the sandbox "
"as well."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1699
msgid ""
"Depending on how Nix was built, the default value for this option may be "
"empty or provide `/bin/sh` as a bind-mount of `bash`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1704
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-chroot-dirs`, `build-sandbox-paths`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1706
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-secret-key-files\">[`secret-key-files`](#conf-secret-key-"
"files)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1708
msgid ""
"A whitespace-separated list of files containing secret (private) keys. These "
"are used to sign locally-built paths. They can be generated using `nix-store "
"--generate-binary-cache-key`. The corresponding public key can be "
"distributed to other users, who can add it to `trusted-public-keys` in their "
"`nix.conf`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1716
msgid "<span id=\"conf-show-trace\">[`show-trace`](#conf-show-trace)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1718
msgid ""
"Whether Nix should print out a stack trace in case of Nix expression "
"evaluation errors."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1723
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-ssl-cert-file\">[`ssl-cert-file`](#conf-ssl-cert-file)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1725
msgid ""
"The path of a file containing CA certificates used to authenticate `https://"
"` downloads. Nix by default uses the first of the following files that "
"exists:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1729
msgid "`/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1730
msgid "`/nix/var/nix/profiles/default/etc/ssl/certs/ca-bundle.crt`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1732
msgid ""
"The path can be overridden by the following environment variables, in order "
"of precedence:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1735
msgid "`NIX_SSL_CERT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1736
msgid "`SSL_CERT_FILE`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1740
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-stalled-download-timeout\">[`stalled-download-timeout`]"
"(#conf-stalled-download-timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1742
msgid ""
"The timeout (in seconds) for receiving data from servers during download. "
"Nix cancels idle downloads after this timeout's duration."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1746
msgid "**Default:** `300`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1748
msgid "<span id=\"conf-start-id\">[`start-id`](#conf-start-id)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1750
msgid "The first UID and GID to use for dynamic ID allocation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1752
msgid "**Default:** `872415232`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1754
msgid "<span id=\"conf-store\">[`store`](#conf-store)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1756
msgid ""
"The [URL of the Nix store](../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to use "
"for most operations."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1759
msgid ""
"See the [Store Types](../store/types/index.md) section of the manual for "
"supported store types and settings."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1763
msgid ""
"Can be overridden by the [`NIX_REMOTE`](../command-ref/env-common.md#env-"
"NIX_REMOTE) environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1765
msgid "The default value is [`auto`](../store/types/index.md#auto)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1767
msgid "**Default:** `auto`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1769
msgid "<span id=\"conf-substitute\">[`substitute`](#conf-substitute)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1771
msgid ""
"If set to `true` (default), Nix uses binary substitutes if available. This "
"option can be disabled to force building from source."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1777
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-use-substitutes`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1779
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-substituters\">[`substituters`](#conf-substituters)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1781
msgid ""
"A list of [URLs of Nix stores](../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to "
"be used as substituters, separated by whitespace. A substituter is an "
"additional [store](../glossary.md#gloss-store) from which Nix can obtain "
"[store objects](../store/store-object.md) instead of building them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1784
msgid ""
"Substituters are tried based on their priority value, which each substituter "
"can set independently. Lower value means higher priority. The default is "
"`https://cache.nixos.org`, which has a priority of 40."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1788
msgid ""
"At least one of the following conditions must be met for Nix to use a "
"substituter:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1790
msgid ""
"The substituter is in the [`trusted-substituters`](#conf-trusted-"
"substituters) list"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1791
msgid ""
"The user calling Nix is in the [`trusted-users`](#conf-trusted-users) list"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1793
msgid ""
"In addition, each store path should be trusted as described in [`trusted-"
"public-keys`](#conf-trusted-public-keys)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1795
msgid "**Default:** `https://cache.nixos.org/`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1797
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `binary-caches`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1799
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-sync-before-registering\">[`sync-before-registering`](#conf-"
"sync-before-registering)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1801
msgid "Whether to call `sync()` before registering a path as valid."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1805
msgid "<span id=\"conf-system\">[`system`](#conf-system)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1807
msgid ""
"The system type of the current Nix installation. Nix only builds a given "
"[store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation) locally when its "
"`system` attribute equals any of the values specified here or in [`extra-"
"platforms`](#conf-extra-platforms)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1810
msgid ""
"The default value is set when Nix itself is compiled for the system it will "
"run on. The following system types are widely used, as Nix is actively "
"supported on these platforms:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1813
msgid "`x86_64-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1814
msgid "`x86_64-darwin`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1815
msgid "`i686-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1816
msgid "`aarch64-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1818
msgid "`armv6l-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1819
msgid "`armv7l-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1821
msgid ""
"In general, you do not have to modify this setting. While you can force Nix "
"to run a Darwin-specific `builder` executable on a Linux machine, the result "
"would obviously be wrong."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1824
msgid ""
"This value is available in the Nix language as [`builtins.currentSystem`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-currentSystem) if the [`eval-system`](#conf-"
"eval-system) configuration option is set as the empty string."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1830
msgid "**Default:** `x86_64-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1832
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-system-features\">[`system-features`](#conf-system-"
"features)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1834
msgid "A set of system “features” supported by this machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1836
msgid ""
"This complements the [`system`](#conf-system) and [`extra-platforms`](#conf-"
"extra-platforms) configuration options and the corresponding [`system`](../"
"language/derivations.md#attr-system) attribute on derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1838
msgid ""
"A derivation can require system features in the [`requiredSystemFeatures` "
"attribute](../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-"
"requiredSystemFeatures), and the machine to build the derivation must have "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1840
msgid "System features are user-defined, but Nix sets the following defaults:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1842
msgid "`apple-virt`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1844
msgid "Included on Darwin if virtualization is available."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1846
msgid "`kvm`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1848
msgid "Included on Linux if `/dev/kvm` is accessible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1850
msgid "`nixos-test`, `benchmark`, `big-parallel`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1852
msgid ""
"These historical pseudo-features are always enabled for backwards "
"compatibility, as they are used in Nixpkgs to route Hydra builds to specific "
"machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1854
msgid "`ca-derivations`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1856
msgid ""
"Included by default if the [`ca-derivations` experimental feature](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-ca-derivations) is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1858
msgid ""
"This system feature is implicitly required by derivations with the "
"[`__contentAddressed` attribute](../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-"
"__contentAddressed)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1860
msgid "`recursive-nix`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1862
msgid ""
"Included by default if the [`recursive-nix` experimental feature](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-recursive-nix) is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1864
msgid "`uid-range`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1866
msgid ""
"On Linux, Nix can run builds in a user namespace where they run as root (UID "
"0) and have 65,536 UIDs available. This is primarily useful for running "
"containers such as `systemd-nspawn` inside a Nix build. For an example, see "
"[`tests/systemd-nspawn/nix`](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"blob/67bcb99700a0da1395fa063d7c6586740b304598/tests/systemd-nspawn.nix)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1871
msgid ""
"Included by default on Linux if the [`auto-allocate-uids`](#conf-auto-"
"allocate-uids) setting is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1875
msgid "<span id=\"conf-tarball-ttl\">[`tarball-ttl`](#conf-tarball-ttl)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1877
msgid ""
"The number of seconds a downloaded tarball is considered fresh. If the "
"cached tarball is stale, Nix checks whether it is still up to date using the "
"ETag header. Nix downloads a new version if the ETag header is unsupported, "
"or the cached ETag doesn't match."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1882
msgid ""
"Setting the TTL to `0` forces Nix to always check if the tarball is up to "
"date."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1885
msgid "Nix caches tarballs in `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/nix/tarballs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1887
msgid ""
"Files fetched via `NIX_PATH`, `fetchGit`, `fetchMercurial`, `fetchTarball`, "
"and `fetchurl` respect this TTL."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1892
msgid "<span id=\"conf-timeout\">[`timeout`](#conf-timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1894
msgid ""
"This option defines the maximum number of seconds that a builder can run. "
"This is useful (for instance in an automated build system) to catch builds "
"that are stuck in an infinite loop but keep writing to their standard output "
"or standard error. It can be overridden using the `--timeout` command line "
"switch."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1905
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `build-timeout`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1907
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trace-function-calls\">[`trace-function-calls`](#conf-trace-"
"function-calls)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1909
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, the Nix evaluator traces every function call. Nix prints a "
"log message at the \"vomit\" level for every function entrance and function "
"exit."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1918
msgid "The `undefined position` means the function call is a builtin."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1920
msgid ""
"Use the `contrib/stack-collapse.py` script distributed with the Nix source "
"code to convert the trace logs in to a format suitable for `flamegraph.pl`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1926
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trace-import-from-derivation\">[`trace-import-from-"
"derivation`](#conf-trace-import-from-derivation)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1930
msgid ""
"When this setting is `true`, Nix logs a warning indicating that it performed "
"such an import. This option has no effect if `allow-import-from-derivation` "
"is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1935
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trace-verbose\">[`trace-verbose`](#conf-trace-verbose)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1937
msgid ""
"Whether `builtins.traceVerbose` should trace its first argument when "
"evaluated."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1941
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trust-tarballs-from-git-forges\">[`trust-tarballs-from-git-"
"forges`](#conf-trust-tarballs-from-git-forges)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1943
msgid ""
"If enabled (the default), Nix considers tarballs from GitHub and similar Git "
"forges to be locked if a Git revision is specified, e.g. `github:NixOS/"
"patchelf/7c2f768bf9601268a4e71c2ebe91e2011918a70f`. This requires Nix to "
"trust that the provider returns the correct contents for the specified Git "
"revision."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1950
msgid ""
"If disabled, such tarballs are only considered locked if a `narHash` "
"attribute is specified, e.g. `github:NixOS/"
"patchelf/7c2f768bf9601268a4e71c2ebe91e2011918a70f?narHash=sha256-"
"PPXqKY2hJng4DBVE0I4xshv/vGLUskL7jl53roB8UdU%3D`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1956
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trusted-public-keys\">[`trusted-public-keys`](#conf-trusted-"
"public-keys)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1958
msgid "A whitespace-separated list of public keys."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1960
msgid ""
"At least one of the following condition must be met for Nix to accept "
"copying a store object from another Nix store (such as a [substituter](#conf-"
"substituters)):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1964
msgid "the store object has been signed using a key in the trusted keys list"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1965
msgid "the [`require-sigs`](#conf-require-sigs) option has been set to `false`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1966
msgid "the store URL is configured with `trusted=true`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1967
msgid ""
"the store object is [content-addressed](../glossary.md#gloss-content-"
"addressed-store-object)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1969
msgid ""
"**Default:** `cache.nixos.org-1:6NCHdD59X431o0gWypbMrAURkbJ16ZPMQFGspcDShjY=`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1971
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `binary-cache-public-keys`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1973
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trusted-substituters\">[`trusted-substituters`](#conf-"
"trusted-substituters)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1975
msgid ""
"A list of [Nix store URLs](../store/types/index.md#store-url-format), "
"separated by whitespace. These are not used by default, but users of the Nix "
"daemon can enable them by specifying [`substituters`](#conf-substituters)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1978
msgid ""
"Unprivileged users (those set in only [`allowed-users`](#conf-allowed-users) "
"but not [`trusted-users`](#conf-trusted-users)) can pass as `substituters` "
"only those URLs listed in `trusted-substituters`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1982
msgid "**Deprecated alias:** `trusted-binary-caches`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1984
msgid ""
"<span id=\"conf-trusted-users\">[`trusted-users`](#conf-trusted-users)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1986
msgid ""
"A list of user names, separated by whitespace. These users will have "
"additional rights when connecting to the Nix daemon, such as the ability to "
"specify additional [substituters](#conf-substituters), or to import unsigned "
"realisations or unsigned input-addressed store objects."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1989
msgid ""
"You can also specify groups by prefixing names with `@`. For instance, "
"`@wheel` means all users in the `wheel` group."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:1994
msgid ""
