#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2051
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, Nix conforms to the [XDG Base Directory Specification]"
"(https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/basedir-spec-latest."
"html) for files in `$HOME`. The environment variables used to implement this "
"are documented in the [Environment Variables section](../command-ref/env-"
"common.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2056
msgid ""
"**Warning** This changes the location of some well-known symlinks that Nix "
"creates, which might break tools that rely on the old, non-XDG-conformant "
"locations."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2059
msgid "In particular, the following locations change:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2061
msgid "Old"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2061
msgid "New"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2063
msgid "`~/.nix-profile`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2063
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profile`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2064
msgid "`~/.nix-defexpr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2064
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/defexpr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2065
msgid "`~/.nix-channels`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2065
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/channels`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2067
msgid ""
"If you already have Nix installed and are using [profiles](../package-"
"management/profiles.md) or [channels](../command-ref/nix-channel.md), you "
"should migrate manually when you enable this option. If `$XDG_STATE_HOME` is "
"not set, use `$HOME/.local/state/nix` instead of `$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix`. This "
"can be achieved with the following shell commands:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/conf-file.md:2072
msgid "${XDG_STATE_HOME-$HOME/.local/state}/nix"
msgstr ""

